GOL-3005: kill the run's process group when a run exits.

Target: EngineeringMoonBear/Paperclip-AgenticOS @ agenticos-v0.2.1 (the pin in
infra/cloud-init/droplet-bootstrap.yaml.tpl).
Upstream status: NOT upstreamed — the agenticos-developer App is not installed on
that owner, so agent automation cannot PR the fork. See ../paperclip-patches/README.md.

Agent runs left LIVE processes behind: during the GOL-3002 pid audit, 14 live
chrome processes (160 threads) were still running inside paperclip-server from
runs that had already ended. Run children are already spawned detached (own
process group) and the timeout/cancel paths already signal the group, but the
ordinary exit paths only dropped the in-memory handle, so anything that outlived
the run leader survived indefinitely against pids_limit: 2048 and mem_limit: 3g.

This adds packages/adapter-utils/src/leftover-process-group.ts (self-contained,
no imports beyond node:fs) and calls it from the close/error handlers of
runChildProcess: SIGTERM the group, SIGKILL after a bounded grace, no-op when
nothing is still running.

Note kill(pid, 0) succeeds on a ZOMBIE, so the sweep scans /proc for group
members whose state is not Z rather than trusting kill(-pgid, 0) alone —
otherwise every clean run would signal itself. And because a SIGKILLed leftover
becomes a zombie, this needs the container init reaper (GOL-3002) alongside it to
actually return the pid; on its own it returns the RAM and the threads.

